  "title": "The Dropped Pencil Relay",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A pupil-like paper figure drops a pencil beyond a row of occupied desks and cannot reach it without disrupting everyone. The nearest figure picks it up and quietly passes it down the row; each recipient points toward the owner until the pencil arrives with a tiny folded paper bow added by the last helper.",
  "hook": "It is yours. Pass it closer.",
  "visible_action": "Pencil rolls; one hand retrieves it; successive hands pass and point; pencil lands on owner’s desk; a small thank-you wave travels back.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Small help can move through a group without becoming a spectacle.",
  "gate": "Use fictional stylized figures, no real minor’s likeness or personal information; keep the object blunt and safely handled.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
